     These functions return the size in bytes of the file representation of
     _c_o_u_n_t numbers of objects of ELF type _t_y_p_e.  For ELF types that are of
     variable length, these functions return a size of one byte.

     Functions eellff3322__ffssiizzee() and eellff6644__ffssiizzee() return sizes for files of class
     ELFCLASS32 and ELFCLASS64 respectively.  Function ggeellff__ffssiizzee() returns
     the size for the class of ELF descriptor _e_l_f.

